        "type": "boolean",
        "default": false,
        "description": "The table's own row identity (SQLite rowid), registered as a column so a keyless table read under rule 1c can be identified. Dialect-specific."
       },
       "path": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
         "type": "string"
        },
        "minItems": 1,
        "description": "The value is not the column but a path to a scalar inside the document it holds (rule 12). `[\"location\", \"city\"]` reads location_metadata -> location -> city. The emitter renders it with fn.jsonPath and casts to dataType; nothing in the query language mentions it, because a role mapped to a path is a role like any other."
       }
      }
     }
